= Interoperability — Simple =

Interoperability is the ability of distinct systems or components to exchange information or services and use the exchanged results according to shared expectations.

Interoperability can depend on compatible protocols, data models, semantics, identifiers, security mechanisms, and operational conventions. Systems do not need identical internal implementations to interoperate.

'''Important boundaries:'''
* interoperability ≠ identical implementation
* data exchange ≠ semantic interoperability automatically

